<title>INDIA: Indian gold eases on profit-taking, sluggish demand.</title>
<headline>Indian gold eases on profit-taking, sluggish demand.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian gold prices eased on profit-taking and sluggish demand on Monday after a firm opening, dealers said.</p>
<p>Sentiment at the close remained subdued with traders expecting higher arrivals through imports in the next few days.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 grammes) opened higher at 59,900 rupees per piece against previous closing of 59,750 rupees but slid thereafter to conclude at 59,800 rupees. Silver on the other hand moved in a narrow range and finished on a quiet note amid limited activity.  </p>
